10. BACKGROUND JOB PROCESSING
==================================================

Implement a background worker to release expired reservations.

Preferred implementation:
- Redis
- BullMQ
- A separate Node.js worker process
- Periodic scheduled cleanup as a recovery mechanism

The worker must:
1. Find ACTIVE or otherwise eligible expired reservations.
2. Claim them safely to avoid duplicate processing.
3. Start a database transaction.
4. Lock the reservation and related inventory records.
5. Recheck the reservation status and expiration time.
6. Mark the reservation EXPIRED.
7. Release the held inventory.
8. Commit the transaction.

The process must be idempotent.

If the worker crashes, the job should be retried safely.

Add structured logs and error handling.

Do not rely only on an in-memory setTimeout because it will not reliably survive server restarts or multiple server instances.

Provide a periodic database cleanup or reconciliation task so missed jobs can be recovered.

